{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_LtCjM1I3ZSVk1Ra4aXoCC7qn","content":"1\t# pace-bot\n2\t\n3\tA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\n4\tby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\n5\tprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\n6\tthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\n7\twhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\n8\tremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\n9\tits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n10\t\n11\tRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\n12\tmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n13\t`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\n14\tRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\n15\tprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\n16\tmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache."}
